  biomeName: The Glass Plains
  minDepthMeters: 9275
  maxDepthMeters: 9800
  shortDescription: Quenched obsidian sheets at trench depth.
  isPlaceholder: 0
  visitPurpose: Late-game pressure biome. Come here only for major progress, rare
    extraction, and to keep orientation in soft terrain and hunt hidden value.
  commonRewardHook: Even routine value here comes from Abyssal Crystal and Thermal
    Gel.
  rareRewardHook: 'The reason to risk the trip is: Tungsten Chunk and Abyss Pressure
    Shell.'
  landmarkIdentity: The Glass Plains reads through dunes, plains, void cuts, and
    shape changes in the floor. Landmarks should feel singular and intimidating.
  safePocketIdentity: Safe pockets are rare and temporary. Retreat routes matter
    more than comfort.
  riskSummary: 'Main failure mode: orientation loss and long empty recovery swims,
    depth stress, and expensive hesitation. Creature pressure stays extreme.'
  extractionFocus: 'High-risk extraction under thermal and survival pressure. Deep
    tier: accept longer sweeps and weaker orientation during gathering, extract only
    what justifies the risk, and leave cleanly.'
  landmarkGuidance: Dominant landmark is magma seam or hadal chimney crown. This
    slot should read through red-black catastrophic skyline; use silhouette changes
    to avoid getting lost in soft terrain.
